aok-utouch
==========

The application links QEMU statically, which makes the resulting binary a
covered work under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

QEMU is not vendored in this repository. `scripts/00-fetch.sh` clones

    https://github.com/emkey1/qemu   branch aok-vm   (a fork of QEMU 11.1.2)

and `versions.env` (written by that script, committed by CI) pins the exact
commit each build used. That commit, together with the unmodified upstream
sources and the two edits the script applies (documented inline in
`scripts/00-fetch.sh`: renaming `main()` in `system/vl.c`, and nothing else),
is the complete corresponding source for the engine in any binary we ship.

Also linked or embedded:

  glib, pixman, pcre2, libffi     LGPL-2.1+ / MIT / BSD / MIT
  edk2 (pflash firmware blobs)    BSD-2-Clause-Patent
  Ubuntu 24.04 userland           various free licences, shipped as a disk image
  Lomiri / Ubuntu Touch packages  GPL-3.0, LGPL-3.0, various

Each is used unmodified from its upstream release archive or distribution
package; the download URLs and versions are in `deps/manifest.env` and
`scripts/20-make-ut-image.sh`.

The gadget sources under `tcg/` and `target/*/tcg/aok/` in the engine are
GPL-2.0-or-later, a dual grant from iSH-AOK that exists so QEMU (GPLv2) can
build them. See `emkey1/aok-gadgets` README for the provenance.
